earthview-wallpaper (2.2.0) stable; urgency=high

  * Add Wikimedia Commons as a source: roughly 1,600 peer-reviewed landscape
    and astronomy photographs from Featured pictures and Quality images
    categories, at 4-6K native resolution, requiring no API key. The listing
    is cached for a week because Commons rate limits repeated requests.
  * No image identifiers are stored in the code any more. Every source now
    discovers its images at run time, through a search, an archive index or a
    category listing.
  * Restore Unsplash usefully by switching it to live search with an API key.
    Diagnostics on the previous bundled list found 33 of 36 images were in
    fact good, so removing all of them in 2.1.1 was an overcorrection; the
    list is gone regardless, since identifiers no longer live in the code.
  * Send a descriptive User-Agent when downloading. Requests sends none by
    default, and Wikimedia answers that with 403, so Commons images could not
    have been downloaded at all.
  * Remove three collection entries whose URLs return 404. All 26 remaining
    collection images were verified to resolve.

 -- Alper Sakarya <earthview@example.com>  Mon, 17 Aug 2026 10:15:00 +0000

earthview-wallpaper (2.1.1) stable; urgency=high

  * Stop Unsplash serving unrelated photographs, including portraits of
    people. The bundled list of Unsplash photo identifiers was not verified
    against the images it referenced, so entries labelled as scenery pointed
    at arbitrary photos. That list has been removed rather than corrected,
    since its metadata could not be trusted.
  * Unsplash now requires a free API key and reports itself unavailable
    without one, so it is skipped instead of substituting arbitrary images.
    No keyless access remains: the internal search endpoint refuses non
    browser clients, source.unsplash.com is retired, and the documented API
    rejects unauthenticated requests. The previous keyless search path had
    therefore never worked, and every Unsplash wallpaper came from the
    unverified list.
  * Screen Unsplash results against their description and tags, rejecting
    people-centric photos, which the service returns freely for queries
    about landscapes.
  * A source lock that cannot be satisfied, such as locking to Unsplash with
    no key configured, now falls back to the available sources instead of
    leaving the wallpaper frozen. The tray menu marks sources needing a key
    and warns when a lock is unusable.

 -- Alper Sakarya <earthview@example.com>  Mon, 17 Aug 2026 10:00:00 +0000

earthview-wallpaper (2.1.0) stable; urgency=medium

  * Add a source lock. A new "Lock to Sources" tray submenu restricts
    automatic and manual changes to a chosen source, or several, so it is now
    possible to run only Unsplash, or only the live satellites. Selecting
    "All Sources" or clearing the selection returns to using everything.
  * Locked sources rotate evenly among themselves, and no image still repeats
    within seven days.
  * The Preferences source checkboxes now share these semantics. Previously
    ticking one box while none were recorded silently restricted the app to
    that single source, and unticking the last box left nothing usable.
  * Clearing the lock in Preferences now takes effect immediately instead of
    leaving the previous restriction applied until restart.
  * "Change From Source" continues to ignore the lock, since it is an explicit
    one-off request.

 -- Alper Sakarya <earthview@example.com>  Wed, 12 Aug 2026 15:00:00 +0000

earthview-wallpaper (2.0.6) stable; urgency=high

  * Fix a package that could not start at all. The 2.0.4 and 2.0.5 builds
    omitted logsetup.py, so the installed application aborted immediately
    with "ModuleNotFoundError: No module named 'logsetup'". The build staged
    modules from a hardcoded list which was not updated when that module was
    added; it now copies every module by glob.
  * The build verifies that each source module is present in the finished
    archive and that the entry point's imports all resolve, then discards the
    archive if either check fails.
  * Start the application after installation. A fresh install launches it for
    every user with an active graphical session, while an upgrade only
    restores users who had it running, so anyone who deliberately quit is
    left alone.
  * Detect the target user's display from their running session instead of
    assuming :0. Under dpkg the DISPLAY variable is unset, so the previous
    fallback would fail on any system whose display is not :0.

 -- Alper Sakarya <earthview@example.com>  Wed, 12 Aug 2026 14:50:00 +0000

earthview-wallpaper (2.0.5) stable; urgency=medium

  * Replace the application icon with original artwork. The previous icon was
    derived from Google imagery; the new one is a hand-authored SVG globe with
    orbital arcs and viewfinder framing, carrying no third party branding.
  * Install icons at 32, 48, 64, 128, 256 and 512 pixels plus a scalable SVG,
    so desktop environments can pick the size they need instead of rescaling
    a single bitmap.
  * Icon artwork now lives in packaging/icons and is staged at build time, so
    the installed theme cannot drift from the master files.

 -- Alper Sakarya <earthview@example.com>  Wed, 12 Aug 2026 14:45:00 +0000

earthview-wallpaper (2.0.4) stable; urgency=high

  * Add file logging to ~/.cache/earthview/earthview.log with rotation, a
    "View Log" menu entry, and a --debug flag. Source and provider failures
    are now recorded instead of being written to a discarded stdout.
  * Fix a black desktop after upgrading from 2.0.2 or earlier. Those versions
    stored the wallpaper inside the installation directory, which is removed
    on upgrade, leaving the desktop pointing at a missing file. The app now
    detects a wallpaper setting that points nowhere and repairs it, and the
    package clears stale references during installation.
  * Always set both picture-uri and picture-uri-dark. Previously a failure to
    set the dark variant was ignored, so systems in dark mode could keep
    showing a stale or missing image.
  * Reject downloads under 1KB rather than applying them, since a truncated
    response or error page renders as a black desktop.

 -- Alper Sakarya <earthview@example.com>  Wed, 12 Aug 2026 14:40:00 +0000

earthview-wallpaper (2.0.3) stable; urgency=medium

  * Fix location mode collapsing onto a single source. Fly-over "location"
    mode filtered to sources advertising geographic support, which only
    Google Earth View does, so every wallpaper came from that one source.
    All sources now participate in location mode.
  * Widen the Google Earth View geographic candidate pool from 5 to 40+
    entries, which caused the same few nearby places to repeat endlessly.
  * Retarget GOES imagery at GOES-19; NOAA retired the GOES-16 paths and
    they now redirect. Added 23 verified satellite/sector combinations.
  * Add a time-bucketed parameter to GOES URLs so the live feed is not
    treated as a single image by deduplication.
  * Draw NASA EPIC imagery from the full ~3592 date archive instead of
    only the most recent capture.
  * Stop retrying sources that report failure, which was exhausting the
    shared NASA APOD demo key quota.
  * Write the downloaded wallpaper to ~/.cache/earthview/ instead of the
    installation directory, so /usr/share can stay read-only.
  * Package now stops running instances before upgrade or removal and
    restarts them afterwards, cleans stale bytecode, and installs with
    root ownership.

 -- Alper Sakarya <earthview@example.com>  Wed, 12 Aug 2026 14:30:00 +0000

